{
  "dom_id": "step-q184783",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Let $n$ be an integer. Using the contrapositive, prove that $n$ is odd provided that $7n+6$ is odd.\n\nThe contrapositive form of the given statement is as follows:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\,⇒\\,{{field-2}}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this statement instead of the original one.\n\nIf $n$ is {{field-3}}, then $n=$ {{field-4}} for some integer $a.$",
